I've written the assessment to session_plan/assessment.md (about 11 KB). Nothing was committed: session_plan/ is gitignored, so the commit step's git add was refused. I had briefly force-staged the file and then unstaged it, so the working tree is clean apart from that ignored file. The planner reads it from disk.

Build and recent runs: the harness had already confirmed this commit (40dd2644) builds and passes tests, and CI on it is green. The last four evolve runs succeeded, with no reverts in the window. The binary works: yoyo -p answered correctly in both plain and json output. Each of last night's two task titles appears twice in git log; the second commit only adds a line to .yoyo/risk_validations.jsonl, so it isn't duplicated work.

One new gap, found by probing:
• JSON output doesn't escape invisible characters. Claude Code changed this on Oct 26: its --output-format json and stream-json now write DEL, C1 control characters and Unicode format characters (like the right-to-left override U+202E) as \uXXXX.
  • Parsed values don't change, but the raw output becomes safe to show on a terminal.
  • yoyo still writes them raw: a run that read a file containing U+202E put the bytes e2 80 ae straight into the response string.
  • It's a small, product-safe fix at three emission points (src/main.rs:291, src/prompt/stream_session_restored.rs:54, src/prompt/stream_external_servers.rs:34).
  • It has no issue yet, so the planner should file one with the task.

Already-filed bugs that still reproduce at 40dd2644:
• #1091: yoyo grep hello a b searches one path called a b and exits 2.
• #1088: yoyo watch "echo hi" announces watch mode is on, exits 0, and the setting dies with the process.
• #1086: shell subcommands print REPL-style usage (usage: /find, /run … or !<command>).
• #1083: yoyo doctor's Curl row mentions /docs and /web, which only exist inside a session.

Research: the Oct 26 Claude Code release has fixes in two classes I'd already filed myself:
• #1057: a worktree removed while a background helper still works in it. Claude Code fixed the same thing for its subagents, which backs my bug report; it can lose data.
• #1088: messages that promise something that isn't coming.

Codex 0.163 added parallel read-only tools and the ability to steer it while it's answering. Both are too big for one session. I saved the mapped findings to yopedia.

Priorities I suggested to the planner (my read, not a plan):
• Product tasks: the JSON escaping fix, plus one of #1091, #1088 or #1057.
• Evolve task: the experiment already written up on #1041. Kill a stub MCP server after it connects and compare replies with and without the "server exited" note. This tests whether a model really reads a missing tool as "doesn't exist", which two shipped notes assume and nobody has measured.
• #1089, a community suggestion that I do outreach on X and other people's repos: reply in the thread rather than plan a task. Writing to other projects in my name is @yuanhao's decision.
• Avoid anything that needs protected files (#1078, #1071).
